 (report . "Round 7 review (independent, read-only VERIFY subagent) returned REQUEST_CHANGES with one blocking contradiction: the retained verify-chain capture recorded a provenance note that the SHA256SUMS entry for rollback-drill.json no longer matched the committed bytes, because the chain had been executed before SHA256SUMS was rebound, so the capture froze a transient state and contradicted the validation record's claim that SHA256SUMS binds all six files. It was fixed by re-running the whole declared chain with SHA256SUMS already consistent for every bound file (so the lint records no drift) and then rebinding the capture's own SHA256SUMS line to the committed capture; sha256sum -c now passes for all six files and the only provenance notes left for this artifact dir are the two pre-existing benign 'canonical form not enforced on historical artifacts' notes. The reviewer's non-blocking observation was also applied: the report's head label is now 'Repaired code / drill head' with the distinction from the evidence-bound implementation head stated explicitly. The drill transcript, the structured eager-fallback-ms block and the report prose all agree on 472/481/480 ms; the drill artifacts name the repaired code head ba35b090f78f00cc287133f2b77792fa836919cd and are carried forward to the implementation head recorded here. The round-3 through round-6 fixes were confirmed present, including the restore record running after the bounded eager gate with committed dataflow-order tests. The fresh retained chain is green (184 focused tests, arch 32/32, security 64/64, workflows 33/33, check-deps, metrics --lint, provenance lint, fast 1208/1208). The trio is bound at implementation head dd18e1560e91ee8243dbc787eba9734f101f2849 with content digest 7dc6e9fd268b284ab5302c2ffe600258fac060244b7ca9574bf8f94f9bb16140. History: the earlier rounds (producer input, zero-module run, linear history; W2 hygiene; lane wiring; the off-lane eager gate and honest W4 telemetry; stale artifact heads; record-before-gate ordering and drill-timing single-sourcing) were all fixed and are recorded in the red-first captures and the repair narrative."))